  "narrative": {
    "intro": "This page covers federal contract obligations in Connecticut for FY2026 to date. The state has $18.4B in total obligations across 24,365 awards, with an average award size of $753K. Obligations are down 47.8% year over year. The current-year totals are partial because these figures cover fiscal year to date only. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer in the state, and a small group of vendors and industries account for the largest shares of obligation dollars. Use these totals to understand scale and concentration in Connecticut federal contracting without treating the numbers as a full-year picture.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What drove spending in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $18B in Connecticut in FY2026 to date. Obligations are concentrated in a few large vendors and programs, which explains why total obligations reached $18.4B while the DoD share was $18B. Obligations are down 47.8% year over year, reflecting a smaller fiscal-year-to-date total compared with prior years."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and industries dominate contracting in Connecticut?",
        "body": "ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION received $10.8B in obligations and RTX CORPORATION received $3.8B in FY2026 to date. Engineering Services ($7B), Ship Building and Repairing ($3.9B), and Aircraft Manufacturing ($3.2B) are the largest industries by obligations, showing how defense manufacturing and engineering lead Connecticut contracting."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Connecticut?",
      "a": "Connecticut received $18.4B in federal contract obligations as of FY2026 to date. The state reached $18.4B across 24,365 awards with an average award size of $753K. These totals are partial because they cover fiscal year to date only."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Connecticut?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense awards the most contracts in Connecticut, having obligated $18B in FY2026 to date. The next largest buyers are the Department of Homeland Security ($119M) and the Department of Veterans Affairs ($111M)."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest federal contractors in Connecticut?",
      "a": "ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION is the largest federal contractor in Connecticut, with $10.8B in obligations in FY2026 to date. Other large contractors include RTX CORPORATION ($3.8B) and SIKORSKY AIRCRAFT CORPORATION ($2.8B)."
